      "source_model": {
        "about": "What defines this contract, read off the donor file itself at init: GFS v16's NetCDF surface analysis (FV3GFS, gaussian grid) from its Noah land model, four soil layers 0-10/10-40/40-100/100-200 cm, STATSGO soil and IGBP vegetation classes. A donor that does not show every one of these is another GFS land setup (a GFS upgrade to another land model, soil layering or class set): the init keeps its cold-start soil (native MPAS-A) and its receipt and log name what differed; --soil-remap on refuses instead. There is no end date, so an unchanged GFS keeps the contract. THE BREAKAGE THIS PREVENTS: GFS v16 Noah's hydraulics applied to another land model's soil. It replaces valid_through 2026-10-28, the day this table was written, which refused every GFS init after that date on the Noah land model (the WOOF gpuwm 2.9.10 / gpuwm-hex 0.4.10 switch candidate, 2026-10-31).",
        "first_cycle": "2021-03-22T12",
        "first_cycle_reason": "GFS v16's first cycle. Earlier GFS (v15) wrote its surface analysis as nemsio, so no NetCDF donor exists for those cycles: init-source does not ask for one and the init keeps its cold-start soil.",
